			"notes": "## Stockpile 0.3.2\n\nA client-side Fabric mod for Minecraft 26.2 and 26.3 that brings your storage inventory and schematic material checks to a local browser dashboard.\n\n### Changes\n- Added a recipe-substitution toggle to the build planner.\n- Supports vanilla crafting and stonecutting, including chained recipes and batch leftovers.\n- Shares ingredients across the build to prevent counting the same supplies twice.\n- Added an ordered crafting checklist with CSV export.\n- Fixed the crash when opening Stockpile settings through chat.\n- Corrected stair-icon orientation and upgraded all 97 stair icons to 128px.\n\n### Storage features\n- Separate storage and Ender Chest views.\n- Filters for chests, barrels, placed shulkers, and Ender Chests.\n- Tracks items inside packed shulker boxes.\n- Labels placed shulkers and shows their coordinates.\n- Configurable startup hints, key binding, and automatic browser opening.\n\n### Installation\n1. Install Fabric Loader 0.20.1+ and Fabric API matching your Minecraft version.\n2. Download the matching Stockpile build and extract the JAR if needed.\n3. Replace the old Stockpile JAR in your mods folder.\n4. Launch Minecraft and run `/stockpile start`.\n5. Click the dashboard link in chat.\n\nUse `/stockpile settings` to configure the mod. `/stockpile stop` or `/stop` pauses local tracking.\n\n### Notes\n- Counts update while tracked containers are open and when they close. Reopen closed containers to refresh external changes.\n- Hosted inventory imports are snapshots.\n- Recipe substitutions cover vanilla crafting and stonecutting. Smelting, fuel, and custom server recipes are excluded."
		}
